{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The border is a hard 32-action timer: fresh clones become terminal exactly when it is exhausted. That makes the intended solution highly structured. Opening the gates is reproducible, but merely entering the left dock is not the win; I’m now checking whether the cross is a reversible size toggle when submitted inside the dock, which would explain both the 4×4 dock geometry and the nearby 2×2 inset."}}
